::U2UA_L4_Q01::Flexibility is best defined as {=the available range of motion at a joint~the ability to sustain aerobic activity~the force a muscle produces~movement speed}

::U2UA_L4_Q02::Mobility is best defined as {=the ability to control movement through an appropriate range~holding any stretch as far as possible~resting after exercise~maximum joint looseness}

::U2UA_L4_Q03::Which statement accurately compares flexibility and mobility? {=They overlap, but mobility emphasizes controlled usable movement.~They are always identical.~Mobility means more range is always better.~Flexibility measures muscular endurance.}

::U2UA_L4_Q04::The best first part of a general warm-up is usually {=low-intensity whole-body movement~a maximal sprint~a long painful stretch~complete rest}

::U2UA_L4_Q05::An activity-specific warm-up should {=rehearse movements and demands of the upcoming activity~avoid all movements used later~replace the entire activity~begin at maximum intensity}


